                    <msContents>
                        <summary>
                            
                            <p>This is a collection of some fragmentary pieces of writing of about the 13th century A.D. The inscription of which these should have formed parts, is dated in the reign of a certain Tribhuvanachakravartin . . . . . . . and seems to register a gift of land as <hi rend="italic">Tirumaḍaippaḷḷippuṟam</hi> to the temple of Vēdanāyaka-perumāḷ on the hill at Tiruvāraikkal, and gives the names of some benificiaries of the gift. </p>						
                            
                        </summary>
                    </msContents>
